        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A suspension of DyCl3·6H2O (0.125 mmol) and o-vanillin (0.25 mmol) in DMF/CH2Cl2 (5 mL/25 mL) was treated with Et3N (0.5 mmol). The solution was stirred for 1 min, then N2H4·H2O (0.5 mmol) was added. The pale-yellow solution was stirred a further 15 min, filtered, and the filtrate left undisturbed. After 2 days, rectangular orange-yellow crystals of 1 formed. The msh and bmh ligands form in situ from o-vanillin and hydrazine under basic conditions that also generate bridging hydroxides. Crystals were kept in contact with the mother liquor to prevent deterioration.",
